H7609.def:
A woman of the tribe of Ephraim living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 7:24; 
daughter of: Beriah (H1283H); 
sister of: Rephah (H7506) and Resheph (H7566) 
§ Sherah = "kinswoman"
daughter of Ephraim and foundress of the Beth-horons and of a town called after her Uzzen-sherah

H7610.def:
A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Ésaïe 7:3; 
son of: Isaiah (H3470A); 
brother of: Maher-shalal-hash-baz (H4122) 
§ Shear-jashub = "a remnant shall return"
a symbolical name for the son of Isaiah the prophet

H7615.def:
Someone descended from Sheba who was a man of the Cushites living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 10:7; 
son of: Raamah (H7484); 
brother of: Dedan (H1719B); also called Sabean at Job 1:15; 3x
Group of she.va (שְׁבָא "Sheba" H7614) 
§ Sabeans = "drunkard" or "he who is coming"
the people of the nation of Sheba

H7619G.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 23:16; 
son of: Gershom (H1647); 
father of: Jehdeiah (H3165); also called Shubael at 1 Chroniques 24:20; 
§ Shebuel or Shubael = "captive of God"
1) son of Gershom and grandson of Moses
2) one of the 14 sons of Heman the musician

H7619H.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 25:4; 
son of: Heman (H1968I); 
brother of: Bukkiah (H1232), Mattaniah (H4983H), Uzziel (H5816J), Jerimoth (H3406L), Hananiah (H2608P), Hanani (H2607H), Eliathah (H0448), Giddalti (H1437), Romamti-ezer (H7320), Joshbekashah (H3436), Mallothi (H4413), Hothir (H1956) and Mahazioth (H4238); also called Shubael at 1 Chroniques 25:20;
§ Shebuel or Shubael = "captive of God"
1) son of Gershom and grandson of Moses
2) one of the 14 sons of Heman the musician

H7634.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 8:10; 
son of: Shaharaim (H7842) and Hodesh (H2321); 
brother of: Jobab (H3103J), Zibia (H6644), Mesha (H4331), Malcam (H4445A), Jeuz (H3263), Mirmah (H4821), Abitub (H0036) and Elpaal (H0508) 
§ Shachia = "announcement"
a Benjamite, son of Shaharaim by his wife Hodesh

H7644.def:
A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Rois 18:18; also called Shebnah at 2 Rois 18:18,26; 
§ Shebna = "vigour"
a person of high position in the court of king Hezekiah of Judah; subsequently the secretary of Hezekiah

H7652G.def:
A man of the tribe of Gad living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 5:13; 
son of: Abihail (H0032I); 
brother of: Michael (H4317H), Meshullam (H4918I), Jorai (H3140), Jacan (H3275), Zia (H2127) and Eber (H5677H)
§ Sheba = "seven"
a town in Simeon

H7669.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 2:48; 
son of: Caleb (H3612H) and Maacah (H4601L); 
brother of: Tirhanah (H8647), Shaaph (H8174H) and Sheva (H7724); 
half-brother of: Hur (H2354), Jesher (H3475), Shobab (H7727H), Ardon (H0715), Mareshah@1 Chroniques 2:42 (H4337), Haran (H2771B), Moza (H4162), Gazez (H1495), Jahdai (H3056) and Achsah (H5915H) 
§ Sheber = "breaking"
a Judaite, son of Caleb by his concubine Maachah and of the family of Hezron

H7681.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 23:33; 
father of: Jonathan (H3083J); also called Shagee (KJV: Shage) at 1 Chroniques 11:34;
Another name of sham.mah (שַׁמָּה "Shammah" H8048I) 
§ Shage = "erring"
father of Hannathon the Hararite, one of David's mighty warriors

H7687G.def:
A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Rois 16:34; 
son of: Hiel (H2419); 
brother of: Abiram (H0048H)
§ Segub = "exalted"
1) the youngest son of Hiel the Bethelite who rebuilt Jericho
2) a Judaite, son of Hezron

H7687H.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 2:21; 
son of: Hezron (H2696H) and the daughter_of_Machir (H4353I); 
half-brother of: Ram (H7410), Jerahmeel (H3396), Caleb (H3612H) and Ashhur (H0806); 
father of: Jair (H2971)
§ Segub = "exalted"
1) the youngest son of Hiel the Bethelite who rebuilt Jericho
2) a Judaite, son of Hezron
